(* ConstructiveWorld-Main - calibwin small-step chain: step certificates at the window point n = 17 *)
(** * planb4_calib_chain_step_n17: the Laurent chains of planb4_g1_poleA/poleB 17 cut into 7 block certificates: point 17 carries K = 3n+1 = 52 stepper steps per channel, split into blocks of widths [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 4].  For each channel and block i, a remainder-state literal (block 0 stays symbolic: the numerator state planb4_g1_shp/shm 17) and one Example: the w_i-step readout from that state equals its literal, closed by one vm_compute bite over w_i steps.  A build consumer assembles these through planb4_calib_chain_glue_laur instead of re-biting the whole chain.

    Mission.  the Laurent chains of planb4_g1_poleA/poleB 17 cut into 7 block certificates: point 17 carries K = 3n+1 = 52 stepper steps per channel, split into blocks of widths [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 4].  For each channel and block i, a remainder-state literal (block 0 stays symbolic: the numerator state planb4_g1_shp/shm 17) and one Example: the w_i-step readout from that state equals its literal, closed by one vm_compute bite over w_i steps.  A build consumer assembles these through planb4_calib_chain_glue_laur instead of re-biting the whole chain.

    Dependencies.  zzm1_gauss (zzId carrier); planb4_g1_laur_extract (planb4_g1_laur_go, planb4_g1_shp, planb4_g1_shm, planb4_g1_denw); stdlib QArith, List.

    References.  planb4_g1_laur_extract.v:73-112 (stepper and family faces); zzphi_e_leaf00.v:21-23 (one certificate per leaf precedent); planb4_g1_calibwin_b1.v (the landed naive-bite face this chain decomposes).

    Constructivity.  Every statement is Set-borne (zzId on list Q); each Example is one w_i-step vm_compute bite; every bite carries its own Print Assumptions; no axioms, no admits.

    Build.  coqc -native-compiler no -time -q -Q <this sandbox> "" -Q <tree ConstructiveWorld_Live> "" planb4_calib_chain_step_n17.v (Rocq 9.3.0; cpu_guard_v3 wrapped; products stay in this sandbox, the module tree is read-only). *)

